<title>TURKEY: Turkish stocks expected firmer.</title>
<headline>Turkish stocks expected firmer.</headline>
<text>
<p>0655 gmt -- Istanbul stocks are expected to rise on Thursday but high interest rates and cash shortage may restrain the uptrend, brokers said.</p>
<p>* The IMKB National-100 closed at 1,903 on Wednesday, up 53 points, or 2.79 percent, from Tuesday's close.</p>
<p>* Technical analysts expect the index to move between 1,870 and 1,960.</p>
<p>* Some brokers say foreign investors are buying stocks on the exchange.</p>
